    "body": "When tool selection fails, Memory currently maintains its own selector/read/archive flow. Delegate that orchestration to the Shared collector already present in the recorded snapshot. Keep Memory's selected logs, empty-input behavior, archive paths and hosted completeness output; keep redirected-parent diagnostics separate from Shared's receipts.\n\nThe consumer regression now supplies an outside payload in failed selector output and verifies it is not archived, while local tool logs, original selection status and product logs survive. No snapshot, dependency, package-version or public library changes.\n\nValidation: `bash scripts/ci/test-failure-evidence.sh`, affected `shellcheck -x`, changed-document link checks and `git diff --check` pass on Linux. The fixture covers real installer refusal, full/compact archives, byte/mode/link preservation, retries, rejected stores, redirected parents and partial archive failure. Native macOS and hosted upload/download remain for CI. Prepared host tools were supplied through PATH; no real release effects ran.\n\nPrepared against main `3f803533f1` in an isolated clone; the maintainer's normal checkout and pending adoption work are untouched. Pending changelog notes use 0.49.2 without changing package metadata.\n",
